WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:00.834 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-How are you?

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:01.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know what?
I'm doing very well.

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:03.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
The last time I came here,
I won the Booker Prize.

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:06.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-I bought some Mega Millions.

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:06.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You did.
-Yeah, so...

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.242
-Oh, for this time, you think
it's going to be the same thing.

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:12.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is good luck to see me?
-I need a New York house.

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:14.447
-You need a New York -- Yeah.
Well, you might need to buy

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:16.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
a couple Mega Millions, then.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:20.186
Usually one lottery winning will
not buy you a house in New York.

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:22.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you were here in 2015.
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:24.924
-We talked about your book.
You won the Man Booker Prize.

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:27.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did that --
You posted about it.

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:28.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
I did not know
what it looked like

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:30.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
until I saw it
on your Instagram.

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:32.966
There you see, there, and
you wrote, "Holy [Bleep],"

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:36.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
which I think is about right.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:38.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
And does that -- You know --
[ Applause ]

00:00:38.505 --> 00:00:40.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's a big deal
in the literary world.

00:00:40.774 --> 00:00:42.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did it change your life
right away?

00:00:42.442 --> 00:00:47.080 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it did because then any
rude Facebook posts I made

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:48.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
became headlines.
-Oh, I gotcha.

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:51.684
-I -- You know, I went to India,
and the whole time,

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:56.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was tweeting on Facebook
about how bad the airport was.

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:58.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
And by the time I landed,
it was,

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:01.127 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Man Booker Prize winner
insults India."

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:02.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow!
-Yeah.

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:03.263 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That's not great.

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:04.998 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was going on
for the whole week.

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:05.799 line:92%
The best one was at the end,

00:01:05.799 --> 00:01:08.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
when somebody asked me
how am I feeling about Jaipur.

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:10.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "I'm so overwhelmed
by India."

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:13.840
And the thing is, "Marlon James
is overwhelmed by India."

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-And it was, "It seems

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:17.977 align:start size:94% position:6%
he's changed his mind
about India and the Indians."

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:20.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like, "I'm just talking
about your airport."

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:24.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean -- New York.
if we took it personally,

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:25.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
everybody who talked
about LaGuardia,

00:01:25.785 --> 00:01:27.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
none of us are gonna live here
another day.

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:30.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. I mean,
they sued the festival.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really?
-Yeah, I was gonna go

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:34.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
to another festival, and
they were like,

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:36.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You might want to
sit that one out for a year."

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:37.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow. All right.
Well, hopefully,

00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:40.834
you'll be welcome back in India
for your next book.

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:43.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is the first of trilogy.
-Yeah.

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:46.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is already a hefty book.
Do you go into

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:48.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
knowing that you were gonna
write --

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:50.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
because this is wonderful,
but it's long.

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:51.544 line:92%
Do you know when you embark?

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:53.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you say, "This is gonna be
a three-book story"?

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:54.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I knew it was
a three-book story

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:57.750
when I was talking to somebody
about this TV show "The Affair."

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:00.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, that's a Showtime show,
"The Affair"?

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, which I actually
haven't seen yet.

00:02:02.422 --> 00:02:03.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You haven't seen it yet?
Okay.

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:07.760
-But it was hugely influential.
She was -- It was the director,

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:08.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
and she was talking
to me about it

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:11.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
and saying, "This is
a great idea for a TV show."

00:02:11.498 --> 00:02:12.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"Forget the TV show.

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:14.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a great idea
for a trilogy."

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:18.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because in a lot of
African storytelling,

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:20.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
unlike storytelling
in the West,

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:22.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's the trickster
who's telling a story.

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:25.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you already know
you can't quite believe it.

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:26.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, if I put out three books,
which is

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:29.249
three different characters
telling the same story --

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:30.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
by the way, I'm not going to
tell the reader

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:32.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
which one to believe.
They're gonna have to choose

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:34.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
after a few years.
-That's fantastic.

00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:37.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it's gonna explode
all over Reddit.

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:38.925 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:40.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is -- Some people
have called this --

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:43.696
because as you mentioned, this
deals with African folklore --

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:46.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
and some people
have referred to it

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:47.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
as sort of an African
"Game of Thrones"

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
but that actually came from
something you said.

00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:51.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, I said it as
a kind of a joke.

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:53.540 size:84% position:42%
I was talking to one of
your writers backstage.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:55.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
It seems I said it here.
-Oh, really?

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:58.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
So I sent it in, this magazine

00:02:58.645 --> 00:03:01.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
which I honestly didn't think
anybody read.

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:02.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:02.649 --> 00:03:05.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It turns out, all the people
who read it are in media.

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:07.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-And it got so bad

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:09.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
that George R.R. Martin
sent me an e-mail.

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:10.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really?
-Oh, yeah.

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:12.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like, a nice e-mail?
-It was a really nice e-mail.

00:03:12.759 --> 00:03:13.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sent me saying,
"I heard you're writing

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:16.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
an African version of my book
that sounds delightful."

00:03:16.663 --> 00:03:17.897 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:20.366 line:92%
And then he invited me out to --

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:23.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
He invited me out
to his bookstore.

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:24.404 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, that's great.

00:03:24.404 --> 00:03:25.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, so I did
what every writer do.

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:27.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
I say, "Can I get a blurb?"
-Oh, really?

00:03:27.774 --> 00:03:28.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Did you get him to blurb?

00:03:28.841 --> 00:03:32.011
No. He wouldn't blurb you.
-Maybe he just was busy.

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:33.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He was probably busy.
I mean, "Winds of Winter."

00:03:33.313 --> 00:03:35.815
-I got to be honest -- with
all the writing he needs to do,

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:37.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't want him
to waste any time.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:39.719 size:84% position:42%
If I heard he was like,
"Oh, I was trying to,

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:41.788
but I had to read Marlon's book
to blurb him."

00:03:41.788 --> 00:03:43.289 line:92%
-His big 620-page opus, no.

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:45.758
-I will say, one of the things
that I'm gonna take away is,

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:48.228 size:81% position:41%
you keep saying things
either in interviews

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:49.229 line:92%
or on Facebook and forgetting

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:50.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
that people are actually
listening to you,

00:03:50.363 --> 00:03:51.931 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you have to be
a little bit more careful.

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:52.899 line:92%
-I keep forgetting that, yeah.

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:56.536 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You had to do, obviously --
I'm guessing, at least --

00:03:56.536 --> 00:03:58.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
a ton of research,
in reading this.

00:03:58.304 --> 00:04:00.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-How do you even go about --

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:03.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
How many years does it take
to research a book

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:04.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
that is going to be
this specific?

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:06.279 size:88% position:44%
-Well, I mean, it took
two years of research --

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:08.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
meaning, it took two years
of my assistant, Jeff,

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:10.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
to do all the research.
-Okay, gotcha.

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:12.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, this is a Jeff job?
-Yeah.

00:04:12.018 --> 00:04:13.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What do you do while
Jeff's doing the research?

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:16.589 size:78% position:39%
-I -- You know what?
I sit on and I think.

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:19.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-I think very hard.

00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:21.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
[ Applause ]

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:23.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:23.496 --> 00:04:24.731 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Enjoy it, right.

00:04:24.731 --> 00:04:27.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But honestly, I also did --
I did quite a bit of it,

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:30.536 align:start size:94% position:6%
because, I mean, I was
researching for two years --

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:33.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
meaning Jeff was researching
for two years

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:35.008 size:84% position:42% line:92%
before I even wrote ---

00:04:35.008 --> 00:04:38.011 size:78% position:39%
because I didn't know
whose story it was.

00:04:38.011 --> 00:04:39.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm.
-And usually --

00:04:39.078 --> 00:04:41.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is what happens when --
with stories for me.

00:04:41.848 --> 00:04:44.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
I am usually
talking to somebody --

00:04:44.684 --> 00:04:47.153 line:92%
usually a female friend --

00:04:47.153 --> 00:04:49.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I get all my ideas
from women.

00:04:49.022 --> 00:04:52.659
-Not a bad way to go.
-No, and they'll say something.

00:04:52.659 --> 00:04:54.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll go, "That's it."
And when --

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:57.797
You know, when our friend said,
you know, the whole idea

00:04:57.797 --> 00:04:59.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
about "The Affair",
I go, "That was it."

00:04:59.599 --> 00:05:01.734 line:92%
But until then, I didn't know,

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:04.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I sat around in my office
for a good year,

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:07.840
and the idea came
the week before school started.

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:11.177 size:84% position:42%
So, I was like, "Great.
I can write the book.

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:13.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, I got to teach."
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:05:13.246 --> 00:05:18.651
And now, have you already
moved on to the second?

00:05:18.651 --> 00:05:19.819 line:92%
Have you -- Is that part --

00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:20.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I've begun
with the second.

00:05:20.853 --> 00:05:24.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
Of course, the -- the person
who tells book two

00:05:24.257 --> 00:05:26.025 align:start size:94% position:6%
is kind of the villain
of book one.

00:05:26.025 --> 00:05:28.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-So, people already having

00:05:28.561 --> 00:05:30.797 align:start size:94% position:6%
these emotional attachments
to characters,

00:05:30.797 --> 00:05:32.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like, "You might
regret that."

00:05:32.632 --> 00:05:33.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All right.
[ Light laughter ]

00:05:33.766 --> 00:05:35.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
I love the switching
of perspectives.

00:05:35.101 --> 00:05:37.603 line:92%
I know you go to book signings

00:05:37.603 --> 00:05:39.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
where people come to
have you sign their books,

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:41.874 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I heard you were late
to one of them

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:43.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you actually
got caught up

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:44.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
trying to get
one of your books signed.

00:05:44.377 --> 00:05:47.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
So, I'm a huge fan of comics.

00:05:47.013 --> 00:05:48.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm a huge fan of Hellboy.
-Same here. Great.

00:05:48.948 --> 00:05:51.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
A fantastic book.
-It was a L.A. book fair,

00:05:51.818 --> 00:05:54.721
and I had my own line --
I had my own book-signing,

00:05:54.721 --> 00:05:56.723 size:75% position:38%
but Mike Mignola is,
like, right there.

00:05:56.723 --> 00:05:59.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm in this line
that's like half a mile long.

00:05:59.726 --> 00:06:01.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And I'm not leaving,

00:06:01.527 --> 00:06:03.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I have
four stacks of "Hellboy."

00:06:03.696 --> 00:06:06.833 align:start size:94% position:6%
He won't remember any of this.
I'm not leaving,

00:06:06.833 --> 00:06:10.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I came all the way
from Jamaica with the whole --

00:06:10.503 --> 00:06:13.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They should have
run your line up,

00:06:13.506 --> 00:06:15.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, sort of,
perpendicular to his line.

00:06:15.441 --> 00:06:16.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Precisely.
-Yeah.

00:06:16.175 --> 00:06:17.777 size:78% position:39%
They they should have
thought this through.

00:06:17.777 --> 00:06:20.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You -- Now that people

00:06:20.146 --> 00:06:21.647 align:start size:94% position:6%
have read the book,
you can get feedback.

00:06:21.647 --> 00:06:24.183
Do you like those moments where
people can come up to you

00:06:24.183 --> 00:06:25.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
and tell you things
about your book,

00:06:25.618 --> 00:06:27.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
or are there things you dread?
-Not really, no.

00:06:27.286 --> 00:06:29.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, you don't like to go --
-No.

00:06:29.021 --> 00:06:30.423 line:92%
It's -- You know you'll be --

00:06:30.423 --> 00:06:33.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd be at a reading
and it would be great,

00:06:33.226 --> 00:06:34.060 size:88% position:44% line:92%
and then you always have

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:36.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
the, "I don't have a question,
just a comment."

00:06:36.963 --> 00:06:38.698 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:38.698 --> 00:06:40.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I would be like,
"You know what?

00:06:40.099 --> 00:06:42.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
you can comment forever
backstage."

00:06:42.568 --> 00:06:45.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow. There you go.
-I'm pretty good at it now.

00:06:45.304 --> 00:06:46.539 size:78% position:39%
-You're pretty good?
You can shut it down?

00:06:46.539 --> 00:06:48.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I can shut it down.
-That's good.

00:06:48.541 --> 00:06:50.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, I'm very --
I'm just thrilled

00:06:50.476 --> 00:06:52.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you have
another one coming.

00:06:52.011 --> 00:06:54.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I really enjoyed this,
and in general,

00:06:54.147 --> 00:06:55.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's just wonderful having you
back on the show.

00:06:55.348 --> 00:06:58.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thanks so much for being here.
-It's great to be back.

